[{"category":"section","location":"#UnallocatedArrays.jl","page":"Home","text":"(Image: Stable) (Image: Dev) (Image: Build Status) (Image: Coverage) (Image: Code Style: Blue) (Image: Aqua)\n\nA module defining a set of unallocated immutable lazy arrays which will be used to quickly construct tensors and allocating as little data as possible.","title":"UnallocatedArrays.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation-instructions","page":"Home","text":"This package resides in the ITensor/ITensorRegistry local registry. In order to install, simply add that registry through your package manager. This step is only required once.\n\njulia> using Pkg: Pkg\n\njulia> Pkg.Registry.add(url=\"https://github.com/ITensor/ITensorRegistry\")\n\nor:\n\njulia> Pkg.Registry.add(url=\"git@github.com:ITensor/ITensorRegistry.git\")\n\nif you want to use SSH credentials, which can make it so you don't have to enter your Github ursername and password when registering packages.\n\nThen, the package can be added as usual through the package manager:\n\njulia> Pkg.add(\"UnallocatedArrays\")","title":"Installation instructions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Examples","page":"Home","text":"using UnallocatedArrays: UnallocatedArrays\n\nExamples go here.\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"Examples"}]
